# AI Documentation

`docs/ai/` is the normative contract tree. Keep documents timeless and free of progress ledgers.

## Document Classes

- Canonical contracts — current normative behavior
- Feature contracts — subsystem invariants, failure semantics, validation, code maps
- Runbooks — procedures and commands
- Generated references — code-owned registries (do not hand-edit as source of truth)
- Case studies / plans — history only; they do not override contracts

Put each durable rule in one place and link elsewhere. Prefer updating `principles.md` / feature contracts over restating them in `AGENTS.md`.

## Checks

```bash
PYTHONPATH=src python src/tools/check_ai_docs.py
PYTHONPATH=src python src/tools/generate_live_event_registry.py --check
pytest tests/test_ai_docs.py tests/test_live_event_registry_docs.py
```

Router: `docs/ai/README.md`.
